# CODEOWNERS -- Constitutional Runtime
#
# Canonical project-governance copy: policy/governance/CODEOWNERS.
# GitHub only reads CODEOWNERS from .github/, the repository root or docs/, so
# .github/CODEOWNERS is the enforcement copy. The two files must stay identical
# (tests/policy/test_governance.py fails if they drift). Edit both together.
#
# This file does NOT itself enforce anything. Review is only required if the
# repository's branch protection / ruleset for `main` enables "Require review
# from Code Owners". On a solo-owner repository the owner also needs an admin
# bypass (or a second reviewer) to merge their own pull requests; see OPEN_ENDS.md.
#
# Scope [JUDGMENT]: the runtime constitution and its failure semantics, the
# policy package (engine, schemas, governance log), the frozen architecture, the
# development constitution, and this file.

